c63ab8a" 13194139535133 true] [17592186332921 1145 "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩\\text{d}t=⟨\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)={e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t}\\text{d}t={e}^{t}+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{e}^{t}+{c}_{1},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535133 true] [17592186332922 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332923 13194139535133 true] [17592186332922 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332924 13194139535133 true] [17592186332922 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332925 13194139535133 true] [17592186332922 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332926 13194139535133 true] [17592186332922 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332927 13194139535133 true] [17592186332922 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535133 true] [17592186332922 1041 "selection" 13194139535133 true] [17592186332922 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332923 13194139535133 true]